{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhNrt6tJeQfPwngPvpfF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed: `paginate` now returns every item on each page, including a final partial page.\n\n**Cause:** the end index in `src/pagination.ts` was computed as `start + pageSize - 1`, and since `slice` already excludes its end index, every full page lost its last item.\n\n**Change:** one line in `src/pagination.ts`, the end index is now `start + pageSize`. I also dropped the `Math.min(..., items.length)` clamp, since `slice` already stops at the end of the array. Signature and validation are unchanged.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `npm test` passes 4 of 4, but those tests only cover empty input, an out-of-range page and invalid arguments, so they passed before the fix too and don't exercise the bug.\n- An ad hoc check with 7 items and page size 3 returned `[1,2,3]`, `[4,5,6]`, `[7]`, then `[]` for page 4. A page size equal to or larger than the list returned all 7 items.\n\nI did not add a regression test because you asked me not to modify tests; a page-boundary case in `test/pagination.test.ts` would be worth adding. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":344,"cache_read_input_tokens":8674,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":344},"output_tokens":374,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53e4c626-ce78-4373-a482-ae60f56ad7b4","uuid":"c52c83bf-e4ae-4422-873b-0516388d05b3","timestamp":"2026-10-04T14:45:54.883Z","request_id":"req_011CfhNrsgadrvoGpUDfckPQ"}
